{
  "$comment": [
    "T-E2E-ACCOUNT-PREF step 1 \u2014 the per-ACCOUNT Encrypted-mode setting. RESUME-PROTOCOL RULE 30.",
    "DESIGN-E2E-ACCOUNT-PREF.md REV 2 \u00a73 (resolution), \u00a74 (write / no-op / forced reset), \u00a77 (seed).",
    "",
    "LANGUAGE-NEUTRAL. Consumers: tests/e2e-pref-contract.test.mjs (node, the pure functions of",
    "lib/e2ePref-core.js), scripts/e2e-pref-relay-proof.mjs (the SAME change/seed rows against the real",
    "conditional UPDATE in a real Postgres), and \u2014 step 2 \u2014 the Kotlin twin on the android lane.",
    "",
    "row.e2ePref: null = the account never chose (resolves to defaultOn). rev = e2ePrefRev before the op.",
    "resolve.expect: preference = e2ePref ?? defaultOn; effective = preference AND masterEnabled;",
    "  pausedByServer = preference on AND master off (the brake lowers, never raises).",
    "change.expect: changed = the RESOLVED preference moves (master is irrelevant: master=0 still resets);",
    "  revBump 1 and reset true exactly when changed; a no-op writes nothing (storedAfter = row.e2ePref,",
    "  so a null row that re-confirms the default STAYS null).",
    "seed.expect: 'on' only; applies only on a null row; bumps rev when applied (Security M3); never resets.",
    "Rows named in Ken's brief carry named:true; the rest complete the grid."
  ],
